name: Custom.TRUDI.NewLogon
description: |
  TRUDI-managed: detect a new inbound interactive session — the lateral-
  movement signal. Polls established inbound TCP on the SSH port and emits a
  row for any remote source IP not in the baseline allowlist.

  Why the socket, not wtmp/last: key-based non-PTY sshd sessions (how an
  automated pivot lands) never write a utmp/wtmp record, so login-record
  parsers miss them. The ESTABLISHED inbound :22 flow is the reliable signal
  and is also what Custom.TRUDI.Respond.KillSession terminates.

  Demo note: host-forwarded management SSH (TRUDI's own live.*) enters the
  container through the bridge GATEWAY address (x.x.x.1), whereas a genuine
  peer-to-peer lateral session comes from a non-gateway host address. The
  query therefore also excludes gateway (.1) sources so the management plane
  does not self-alert; real lateral movement from a fleet host still fires.

type: CLIENT_EVENT

parameters:
  - name: BaselineLogonSources
    description: JSON array of remote source IPs considered known-good.
    default: |
      ${baseline_logon_sources}
  - name: SshPort
    description: Local port that identifies an inbound SSH session.
    type: int
    default: 22
  - name: PollSeconds
    description: How often to re-snapshot inbound sessions.
    type: int
    default: 10

sources:
  - query: |
      LET baseline <= parse_json_array(data=BaselineLogonSources)
      LET tick = SELECT * FROM clock(period=PollSeconds)
      LET snapshot = SELECT
        timestamp(epoch=now()) AS timestamp_utc,
        Raddr AS remote_ip,
        Rport AS remote_port,
        Laddr AS local_ip,
        Lport AS local_port,
        Status AS state,
        Pid AS pid
      FROM Artifact.Linux.Network.NetstatEnriched()
      WHERE Lport = SshPort
        AND Status = "ESTABLISHED"
        AND Raddr != ""
        AND NOT Raddr =~ "^127\\."
        AND NOT Raddr =~ "\\.1$"
        AND NOT Raddr IN baseline
      SELECT * FROM foreach(row=tick, query=snapshot)
